{"title":"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 48","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_48&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be an equilateral triangle inscribed in circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is a point on arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. \nLines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41ee10c07baa91f100ec2eeca6b7b6ed3ab86698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AM}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02e0af598b1d12c1fc9164924f2c0ead5ea87f30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BM}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/e/cbeda7159b33badd3617a005290a98fb0be341cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CM}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> are drawn. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> is: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/90940759eb28933f2b0e25dbd87de4132b775377.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)); unitsize(2cm); pair O = origin; pair B = (1,0); pair C = dir(120); pair A = dir(240); pair M = dir(90 - 18); draw(Circle(O,1)); draw(A--C--M--B--cycle); draw(B--C); draw(A--M); dot(O); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,E); label(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,NW); label(&quot;$O$&quot;,O,SE);[/asy]\" width=\"215\" height=\"215\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/2/b229467ab9ec8e7406605823d12a20e7d28d651d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{equal to }{BM + CM}\\qquad  \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{less than }{BM + CM}\\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{greater than }{BM+CM}\\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{equal, less than, or greater than }{BM + CM}\\text{, depending upon the position of } {M}\\qquad  \\\\ \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"625\" height=\"77\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_48&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/b/dabcea0e07a3ff88691488c54cc98be26bd0b03c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABMC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> is inscribed in circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, thus it is a cyclic quadrilateral. By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ptolemy%27s_Theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ptolemy&#39;s Theorem\">Ptolemy's Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/d/0cd9e804a70a71ab9f4d595de62ca613d0806c2d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AC \\cdot MB + MC \\cdot AB = BC \\cdot AM.\\]\" width=\"274\" height=\"14\" /> Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is equilateral, we cancel out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> to get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/8/01816cf46befe15140c4d953de4a64c5978dd11a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BM + CM = AM \\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}.\\]\" width=\"241\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_48&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME\" title=\"1957 AHSME\">1957 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?ti